<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trucial Oman Scouts</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1951–1971</span> · Also known as Trucial Oman Levies</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Trucial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> Scouts were a British-officered force raised in 1951 as the Trucial Oman Levies, with headquarters at Sharjah, to keep order in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>. Renamed in 1956, they took part in the Buraimi dispute and in operations in Oman in the late 1950s. In 1971 they were handed over to the new United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> as the core of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-defence-force-united-arab-emirates">Union Defence Force</a>.</p></div>
